{
  "_comment": [
    "Conformance corpus for pkg/celmatch, the hand-written CEL subset that decides",
    "which external CI pipeline may assume a role on the hub.",
    "",
    "Each case records TWO verdicts for the same (expression, claims) pair:",
    "",
    "  cel      - what the reference implementation (cel-go) does. Ground truth,",
    "             produced by testdata/celprobe (see its README) rather than",
    "             recalled from the spec, because the entire failure mode this",
    "             corpus guards against is someone's mental model of CEL being",
    "             wrong in a way they cannot see.",
    "  celmatch - what this package does.",
    "",
    "Verdict domain:",
    "  allow        evaluated to true",
    "  deny         evaluated to false",
    "  error        evaluated, but the evaluation failed",
    "  parse_error  refused before evaluation (CEL: parse/check; celmatch: Compile)",
    "  non_bool     evaluated to a value that is not a bool",
    "",
    "The two columns differ often and that is the design. What must never happen",
    "is celmatch=allow where cel is anything but allow: every caller treats",
    "not-allow as a denial, so cloop being stricter is free and cloop being",
    "looser is an authorization bypass the operator cannot find by re-reading",
    "their own policy. conformance_test.go asserts exactly that, in one",
    "direction, plus both columns cell-by-cell so a future change that flips a",
    "deny into an allow is a test failure and not a discovery.",
    "",
    "Regenerate the cel column with:",
    "  cd testdata/celprobe && go run . -update"
  ],

  "claimsets": {
    "gh_push": {
      "_note": "A real GitHub Actions token for a push to main. Every GitHub-specific claim is a JSON *string* -- including repository_id, actor_id and run_id -- which is the single most load-bearing fact in this corpus. Only iat/exp/nbf are JSON numbers.",
      "sub": "repo:acme/tool:ref:refs/heads/main",
      "repository": "acme/tool",
      "repository_owner": "acme",
      "repository_id": "123456",
      "repository_owner_id": "65",
      "repository_visibility": "private",
      "actor": "dana",
      "actor_id": "12",
      "ref": "refs/heads/main",
      "ref_type": "branch",
      "ref_protected": "false",
      "head_ref": "",
      "base_ref": "",
      "workflow": "release",
      "workflow_ref": "acme/tool/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main",
      "job_workflow_ref": "acme/tool/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main",
      "event_name": "push",
      "run_id": "16055869479",
      "run_number": "33",
      "run_attempt": "1",
      "runner_environment": "github-hosted",
      "iss": "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com",
      "aud": "cloop",
      "iat": 1632493567,
      "exp": 1632493867,
      "nbf": 1632492967
    },

    "gh_env": {
      "_note": "A job that declared `environment: prod`, using the immutable sub format (owner@id/repo@id) that became automatic for new repositories after 2026-07-15.",
      "sub": "repo:acme@99/tool@123456:environment:prod",
      "repository": "acme/tool",
      "repository_owner": "acme",
      "repository_id": "123456",
      "environment": "prod",
      "ref": "refs/heads/main",
      "event_name": "deployment",
      "job_workflow_ref": "acme/tool/.github/workflows/deploy.yml@refs/heads/main",
      "runner_environment": "github-hosted"
    },

    "numeric_id": {
      "_note": "An IdP that emits repository_id as a JSON number instead of a string. Not what GitHub does, but the shape normalize() exists to handle, and the case where a whole float64 must compare equal to an int literal.",
      "repository": "acme/tool",
      "repository_id": 123456,
      "big": 9007199254740993,
      "fractional": 1.5,
      "huge": 1e300,
      "zero_point_zero": 74.0
    },

    "nested": {
      "_note": "Nested claims, for selectNode at every arity plus a missing intermediate at each level.",
      "repository": "acme/tool",
      "ctx": {
        "env": "prod",
        "deep": { "leaf": "value" }
      },
      "shallow": "i-am-a-string",
      "empty": {},
      "groups": ["eng", "release"],
      "mixed": ["eng", 7],
      "mixed_rev": [7, "eng"],
      "nums": [1, 2, 3],
      "flag": true,
      "nothing": null
    }
  },

  "cases": [
    { "group": "baseline", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the happy path" },
    { "group": "baseline", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/other\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "baseline", "expr": "true", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "baseline", "expr": "false", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "baseline", "expr": "assertion.repository", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "a non-bool expression is not a policy" },

    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == 123456", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "THE case the operator gets wrong: GitHub sends repository_id as a string, so the int-literal form an operator naturally writes can never match" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id != 123456", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "negated cross-type: CEL says true here, which is why != on a mistyped claim is the dangerous direction" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == \"123456\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the form that actually works against GitHub" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id != \"999\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.actor_id == 12", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.run_number == 33", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/int-literal-vs-string-claim", "expr": "assertion.run_number != 33", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == \"123456\"", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "mirror image: an IdP that really does send a number" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == 123456", "claims": "numeric_id" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.repository_id != \"123456\"", "claims": "numeric_id" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.zero_point_zero == 74", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "CEL has heterogeneous numeric equality: 74.0 == 74 is true" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.fractional == 1", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "a fractional claim must not round into an int literal" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.fractional != 1", "claims": "numeric_id" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.huge == 1", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "1e300 does not fit an int64; the conversion must not wrap into a match" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/string-literal-vs-int-claim", "expr": "assertion.big == 9007199254740993", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "past float64's exact-integer range: JSON decoding has already lost the low bit" },

    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.ref_protected == false", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "ref_protected is a *stringified* bool in a real token" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.ref_protected == \"false\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.ref_protected != false", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.flag == true", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.flag == \"true\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.repository == true", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "!assertion.repository", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "! on a string" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.repository && true", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "true && assertion.repository", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/bool", "expr": "assertion.repository || true", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"123\" in [123]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "named explicitly in the task: does a string match an int list element" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "123 in [\"123\"]", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [123456]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "string claim against an int allowlist -- the realistic form of the same mistake" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [\"123456\"]", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [123456, \"123456\"]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "a heterogeneous allowlist that does contain a match" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [\"123456\", 999]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "heterogeneous, match comes first" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [999, 998]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "heterogeneous-typed list with no match at all" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository in []", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.ref in [\"refs/heads/main\", \"refs/heads/release\"]", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"release\" in assertion.groups", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"eng\" in assertion.mixed", "claims": "nested", "note": "heterogeneous *claim* list, match is the string" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"nope\" in assertion.mixed", "claims": "nested", "note": "heterogeneous claim list, no match: does the int element poison the search" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "7 in assertion.mixed", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "2 in assertion.nums", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"2\" in assertion.nums", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.repository in assertion.repository", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "`in` against a string, not a list" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"env\" in assertion.ctx", "claims": "nested", "note": "CEL's `in` also tests map keys; the subset has no map membership" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "\"missing\" in assertion.ctx", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.groups == [\"eng\", \"release\"]", "claims": "nested", "note": "list equality" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.groups == [\"eng\"]", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.nums == [1, 2, 3]", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.mixed == [\"eng\", 7]", "claims": "nested", "note": "heterogeneous list equality, element-wise" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/in", "expr": "assertion.mixed == [\"eng\", \"7\"]", "claims": "nested" },

    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the claim a job without an environment: simply does not carry" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "assertion.environment != \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "negation must not turn an absent claim into a pass" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "!(assertion.environment == \"prod\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_env" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "assertion.environment in [\"prod\", \"staging\"]", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "assertion.environment.startsWith(\"pro\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-1", "expr": "assertion.environment.matches(\"^prod$\")", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.ctx.env == \"prod\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.ctx.missing == \"prod\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "present intermediate, absent leaf" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.absent.env == \"prod\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "absent intermediate -- must not panic" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.shallow.env == \"prod\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "selecting a field from a string" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.empty.anything == \"x\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "present but empty map" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.nothing.field == \"x\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "selecting through a null claim" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.groups.env == \"prod\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "selecting a field from a list" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-2", "expr": "assertion.flag.env == \"prod\"", "claims": "nested" },

    { "group": "missing-field/arity-3", "expr": "assertion.ctx.deep.leaf == \"value\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-3", "expr": "assertion.ctx.deep.missing == \"value\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-3", "expr": "assertion.ctx.missing.leaf == \"value\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "missing at the middle of three" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-3", "expr": "assertion.absent.deep.leaf == \"value\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "missing at the root of three" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-3", "expr": "assertion.ctx.env.leaf == \"value\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "string in the middle of three" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-4", "expr": "assertion.ctx.deep.leaf.more == \"x\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "missing-field/arity-4", "expr": "assertion.absent.a.b.c == \"x\"", "claims": "nested" },

    { "group": "missing-field/null", "expr": "assertion.nothing == \"x\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "a claim that is present and null is not an absent claim" },
    { "group": "missing-field/null", "expr": "assertion.nothing != \"x\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "missing-field/null", "expr": "assertion.head_ref == \"\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "head_ref is present-but-empty on a push, not absent" },
    { "group": "missing-field/null", "expr": "assertion.head_ref == \"main\"", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"other/repo\" && assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "false && error: short circuit means the missing claim is never reached" },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.environment == \"prod\" && assertion.repository == \"other/repo\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "error && false: CEL's commutative absorption says false, the subset says error. Both deny." },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" && assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "true && error" },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" || assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "true || error: short circuits to allow in both" },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.environment == \"prod\" || assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "error || true: CEL absorbs to TRUE, the subset errors. This is the one place the subset is stricter in a way an operator could mistake for a bug -- and the direction that keeps it safe." },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.environment == \"prod\" || assertion.repository == \"other/repo\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "error || false" },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"other/repo\" || assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "false || error" },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == 123456 || assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "type-error || true -- the absorption case reached through type confusion rather than a missing claim" },
    { "group": "absorption", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == 123456 && assertion.repository == \"other/repo\"", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.ref.startsWith(\"refs/heads/\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.ref.startsWith(\"refs/tags/\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.job_workflow_ref.endsWith(\"@refs/heads/main\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.job_workflow_ref.contains(\"/.github/workflows/\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.sub.matches(\"^repo:acme/tool:ref:refs/heads/main$\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.sub.matches(\"refs/heads/main\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "unanchored: CEL's matches() is a search, not a full match" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.sub.matches(\"^repo:acme/tool$\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "anchored against a longer subject" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.repository.startsWith(1)", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "non-string argument" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.repository_id.startsWith(\"12\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "works on GitHub's string repository_id" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.repository_id.startsWith(\"12\")", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "same expression, numeric claim: a string method on an int" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.ref_protected.endsWith(\"alse\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.groups.contains(\"eng\")", "claims": "nested", "note": "contains() on a list is not a string method" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.sub.matches(\"^repo:acme@[0-9]+/tool@[0-9]+:environment:prod$\")", "claims": "gh_env", "note": "pinning the immutable sub format" },
    { "group": "strings", "expr": "assertion.sub.startsWith(\"repo:acme/tool:\")", "claims": "gh_env", "note": "a rule written for the legacy sub format, against an immutable-sub token: silently stops matching after a repo transfer" },

    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" && assertion.ref.startsWith(\"refs/heads/\") && assertion.event_name in [\"push\", \"pull_request\"]", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" && assertion.environment == \"prod\" && assertion.runner_environment == \"github-hosted\"", "claims": "gh_env" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" && assertion.environment == \"prod\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the same production rule against a push token: must not admit" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.job_workflow_ref == \"acme/tool/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "pinning the workflow file, the strongest single claim available" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.repository_owner == \"acme\" && assertion.repository_visibility == \"private\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "(assertion.ref == \"refs/heads/x\" || assertion.ref == \"refs/heads/main\") && assertion.actor == \"dana\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.ref == \"refs/heads/x\" || assertion.ref == \"refs/heads/main\" && assertion.actor == \"dana\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "&& binds tighter than || in CEL; a hand-rolled parser that got this backwards would change the meaning of a real rule" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "assertion.ref == \"refs/heads/main\" || assertion.ref == \"refs/heads/x\" && assertion.actor == \"nobody\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "precedence again, arranged so the two readings disagree: (T||F&&F)=true vs ((T||F)&&F)=false" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "!(assertion.repository == \"acme/other\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "!assertion.repository.startsWith(\"evil/\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "! binds tighter than == but looser than a method call" },
    { "group": "realistic", "expr": "(assertion.ref).startsWith(\"refs/\")", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.true == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "CEL reserves `true`; a hand-rolled lexer that treats it as an ordinary field name accepts an expression CEL refuses to parse" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.false == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.null == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.if == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.in == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.for == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.return == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.const == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.void == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/reserved-words", "expr": "assertion.as == \"x\"", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository_id > 1", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "ordering comparison" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository.size() == 9", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.groups.all(g, g == \"eng\")", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.groups.exists(g, g == \"eng\")", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.groups[0] == \"eng\"", "claims": "nested" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository_id + 1 == 2", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" ? true : false", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"a\" == false", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "chained comparison: CEL parses this left-associatively, the subset refuses it" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "has(assertion.environment)", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the macro that exists precisely to make a missing claim testable" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == -1", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "unary minus" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.fractional == 1.5", "claims": "numeric_id", "note": "float literal" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == 0x10", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "hex literal -- not CEL either" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" && (1 == 1)", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "literal-only comparison, no claim involved" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the bare activation variable" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.ctx", "claims": "nested", "note": "a map is not a policy" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "repository == \"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "unqualified claim name: CEL has no such variable declared either" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository.matches(assertion.ref)", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "computed regex -- legal CEL, refused here so a bad pattern is a save-time error" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository.matches(\"[\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "a pattern that does not compile" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.groups in [[\"eng\", \"release\"]]", "claims": "nested", "note": "a list inside a list" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\" // trusted\n", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "CEL has line comments; the subset has no comment syntax" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository_id == 99999999999999999999", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "an int literal past int64" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository in {\"acme/tool\": true}", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "map literal" },
    { "group": "grammar/unsupported", "expr": "assertion.repository.lowerAscii() == \"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push" },

    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "!!(assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "double negation" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "!assertion.repository.startsWith(\"evil/\") && assertion.repository == \"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.repository.contains(\"\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "the empty substring is in every string, in both" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.repository.startsWith(\"\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.sub.matches(\"(?i)REPO:ACME/TOOL\")", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "inline regex flags: both sides are RE2, so a case-insensitive policy must behave identically" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.sub.matches(\"repo:acme/tool:ref:refs/heads/(main|release)$\")", "claims": "gh_push" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.repository == 'acme/tool'", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "single-quoted string" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.ref in [\"refs/heads/main\",]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "trailing comma, which is how a long allowlist gets edited" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.repository\t==\t\"acme/tool\"", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "tabs as whitespace" },
    { "group": "grammar/accepted", "expr": "assertion.empty == \"x\"", "claims": "nested", "note": "an empty map claim compared to a string" },

    { "group": "type-confusion/list-order", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [\"123456\", 999]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "heterogeneous allowlist, match written first" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/list-order", "expr": "assertion.repository_id in [999, \"123456\"]", "claims": "gh_push", "note": "THE SAME allowlist, reordered. A verdict that differs between this and the line above means reordering an allowlist changes who is admitted." },
    { "group": "type-confusion/list-order", "expr": "\"eng\" in assertion.mixed", "claims": "nested", "note": "heterogeneous list from a claim, match BEFORE the odd element" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/list-order", "expr": "\"eng\" in assertion.mixed_rev", "claims": "nested", "note": "the same members, odd element first. Must agree with the line above: a claim list's order is the IdP's choice, not the operator's, so it must not decide the verdict." },
    { "group": "type-confusion/list-order", "expr": "\"release\" in assertion.mixed", "claims": "nested", "note": "same claim list, no match at all: only here may the odd element decide, and it decides to refuse" },
    { "group": "type-confusion/list-order", "expr": "\"release\" in assertion.mixed_rev", "claims": "nested", "note": "no match, odd element first" }
  ]
}
